-36c898bce61e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378247} {:answer/id #uuid "94d62c48-c41c-5fbc-9d7a-f4d1a6557b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378248} {:answer/id #uuid "56d6d423-5656-501e-b2f6-2c600eecf510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fddf6f5d-eb46-55d9-bafa-dfcde8802b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ce217c-40ee-5b1e-ac1e-80701505ad04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "097f179d-8b94-55d4-8f36-ac53f5125474" :question/math-academy-id "q-104930" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\n- $P(N)$\n- $P({Z,\\pi })$\n- $P({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is infinite since the underlying set $N$ is infinite.\n\n- Set II is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,\\pi })={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{\\pi },\\,{Z,\\pi }}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0}={0},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})=P({0})={∅,\\,{0}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054947 :knowledge-p