8982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37ad276a-88ce-596c-9a24-406a32aa6e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-171334" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $10\\ge 1,$ **then** $3\\in R.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If $10<1,$ then $3\\notin R.$\n- If $3\\notin R,$ then $10<1.$\n- If $3\\in R,$ then $10\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d65819f-0528-527e-8d1a-20421e221ca5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Coterminal Angles in Radians" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051050 :topic/math-academy-id 261 :topic/title "Coterminal Angles"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81be9d32-310b-5bd0-93d8-2d3dac4036aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058609} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa9881e-1333-5524-b23a-9511ed369af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058610} {:answer/id #uuid "c3169354-1af9-5571-9187-d8c55358a38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :an